# Bounds the source context `gcloud builds submit` uploads. Terraform's container module runs
# `gcloud builds submit --config docker/cloudbuild.yaml .` from the repo root; the Docker build only
# ever COPYs docker/requirements.txt, so the context genuinely needs nothing but docker/. Without
# this file gcloud falls back to .gitignore, which does NOT exclude src/, notebooks/, configs/, etc.,
# uploading far more than the build needs. This is the ONLY gcloud source-upload path in the repo
# (the seed job uploads src/ via Terraform's archive_file, not gcloud), so scoping to docker/ is safe.
*
!/docker
!/docker/**
